    "industrial_process_notes": "Random copolymerization of styrene (70-80 wt%) and acrylonitrile (20-30 wt%). Higher acrylonitrile content improves mechanical strength and chemical resistance but introduces a yellowish tint. SAN itself later became the base resin for ABS, when polybutadiene rubber particles (10-20 micrometers) are dispersed/grafted into it to add toughness.",
